# Intent: make the wake word and taps robust and visible (owner report 2026-10-21: the robot does not listen, taps do not start or stop listening, and the wake word does not stop it talking). The host log cannot tell what state the unit believes it is in, so: (1) every tap reports its decision (tap: start, stop or ignored, with the DeviceState it saw and why); (2) every wake word detection reports the state it was heard in (wake); (3) once a minute the unit reports the wake-word task's heartbeat and its own state (wake_stats: armed, fetches, fetch_errors, detections, ms_since_fetch, state); (4) a state guard in the one-second clock tick puts a unit that has sat in Connecting for 8 s or in Listening for 45 s back to idle (reported as state_guard), because from those states it cannot hear the wake word and ignores taps; (5) the swipe-down gesture of patch 036 aborted speech whatever the state, which left a listening unit listening with its wake word off after the host had dropped the turn: it now aborts only speech, and ends a listening turn the way a tap does. The detection task stack stays at the stock 4,096 bytes (it is the stock value; 1,852 bytes were left of it in 0.2.25, so it is not overflowing).
# Upstream: 78/xiaozhi-esp32 main/application.cc, main/application.h, main/audio/wake_words/afe_wake_word.cc; m5stack/StackChan firmware/main/hal/board/stackchan_display.cc, hal/hal_head_touch.cpp, hal/device_events.h (MIT). Applies after 058 with --unidiff-zero.
# Check after a flash: tap the face at rest: "unit tap: decision=start state=3"; tap while it listens or speaks: "decision=stop"; say "Hi, StackChan" at rest: "unit wake: state=3" and a turn starts, while it speaks: "unit wake: state=6" and it stops; leave it alone for a minute: "unit wake: wake_stats armed=1 fetches=N" with N in the thousands and state=3. If it ever sits in Connecting or Listening, "unit wake: state_guard" appears and it returns to idle.
